#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119621 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119810 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c8e217c-252d-529f-a810-84787e2ee886" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector is in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "244793f6-41c3-5920-9264-bec32cda9c9c" :question/math-academy-id "e-4807" :question/problem "The matrix $B$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ are given below. \nDetermine if $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Col}(B).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the values of $x_1$ and $x_2,$ where $x_1$ and $x_2$ are the real numbers such that $\\mathbf{b}=x_1\\mathbf{b}_1+x_2\\mathbf{b}_2,$ and $\\mathbf{b}_1,$ $\\mathbf{b}_2$ are the respective columns of $B.$\n\n![](images/a6/a65747aa11107acc9a05df83473ed0208c23818953b16771b608ec4f572dc7ca.svg)" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Col}(B),$ we need to check if the equation $B\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[B \\,|\\, \\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[B\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 15 & -6 & 21 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=7 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get the true statement $0=0.$ So the system is equivalent to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=7 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $x_2=0.$ Substituting into the first equation gives $x_1=\\dfrac 7 5.$ \n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $B\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent, which implies that $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\textrm{Col}(B).$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $\\mathbf{b}$ as a linear combination of $\\mathbf{b}_1$ and $\\mathbf{b}_2\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/8a/8a35321d3a29ee86c5af54e23dabd8d3ac93bf7831981507dff3e501796f96a7.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119622 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119811 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87dc8398-fb5c-564b-a796-db15ff30d72c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector Is in the Column Space of a Larger Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "12f222d8-5563-544a-8154-fb1f9406b231" :question/math-academy-id "e-4808" :question/problem "The matrix $C$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ are given below. Determine if $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Col}(C).$ In affirmative case, find the value of $x_1 \\cdot x_2 \\cdot x_3$, where $x_1$, $x_2$, and $x_3$ are real numbers such that $\\mathbf{b}=x_1\\mathbf{c}_1+x_2\\mathbf{c}_3+x_3\\mathbf{c}_3,$ and $\\mathbf{c}_1,$ $\\mathbf{c}_2,$ and $\\mathbf{c}_3$ are the respective columns of $C.$\n\n![](images/02/027332c5a5bdb14913d297e71bc2ac2ae8f846976c1bc3c0c4c569997dcd5b01.svg)" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Col}(C),$ we need to check if the equation $C\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[C \\,|\\, \\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[C\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3=1$. Substituting into the second equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2}+4(1) & =1 \\\\ 3{x}_{2} & =-3 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =5-{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3} \\\\  & =5-(-1)-4(1) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $C\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent, which implies that $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\textrm{Col}(C).$ \n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $\\mathbf{b}$ as a linear combination of $\\mathbf{c}_1,$ $\\mathbf{c}_2,$ and $\\mathbf{c}_3\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/4c/4cccd67d5e043d72e0b6949543883e6187d9ef807b7a470146628cbadf7eead7.svg)\n\nFinally, we get $x_1 \\cdot x_2 \\cdot x_3 = 2 \\cdot (-1) \\cdot 1 = -2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119670 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119855 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a557ee8d-51a9-5387-a28c-67ffefed55b4" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of an Unknown Given a Vector That’s in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "b6d52e39-a8a0-5048-80a1-a342a2617e0f" :question/math-academy-id "e-6208" :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by ![](images/fd/fdab914fd2a1013caf1d02dc692df697f4c61f61b3aeba6166b471f3833e7811.svg) Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector ![](images/a8/a8acb2b133143150953e861f13e7b9797756c557800b67ca0334a88d26eb3cc9.svg) belongs to $\\textrm{Col}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Col}(A),$ then the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A \\,|\\, \\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2+k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -32 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2+k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -32 \\\\ 0 & -11 & k-48\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -11 & k-48\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+11{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=10 \\\\ {x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 0=k-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k-4,$ which means that $k=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247191 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119811 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87dc8398-fb5c-564b-a796-db15ff30d72c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector Is in the Column Space of a Larger Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05dd1857-2985-546b-9aba-fc98eb855d94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244360} {:answer/id #uuid "20acb5fc-d805-5850-bfb0-2f0f05d25203" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244601} {:answer/id #uuid "2c4cd3b2-1f4e-53be-932d-e0f8f8127322" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244706} {:answer/id #uuid "3940ebec-c39e-553c-b6aa-55bd069457ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244821} {:answer/id #uuid "7d7b3c15-cef9-5072-800b-26138a27eae4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c4cd3b2-1f4e-53be-932d-e0f8f8127322" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244706} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ca7504e-b5bc-5c05-8761-5692c93d71f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246619}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b861c0c2-25f8-5f54-84a3-3dea6f60c30d" :question/math-academy-id "q-110982" :question/problem "The matrix $C$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(C).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}+{x}_{3}{c}_{3},$ and ${c}_{1}$, ${c}_{2}$, and ${c}_{3}$ are the respective columns of $C.$\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -12 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(C),$ we need to check if the equation $Cx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[C\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[C\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & -12 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-8 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=-12 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting it into the second equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}-(2) & =-12 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =-8-3{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} \\\\  & =-8-3(-5)-3(2) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $Cx=b$ is consistent, which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(C).$ \n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${c}_{1},$ ${c}_{2},$ and ${c}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -12 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}=1\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{c}_{1}}+(-5)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{c}_{2}}+2\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{c}_{3}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=1\\cdot (-5)\\cdot 2=-10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120339 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119810 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c8e217c-252d-529f-a810-84787e2ee886" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector is in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bf8b71d-a371-5f81-974e-5142050a5df6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118164} {:answer/id #uuid "b384fbdd-d0d7-5c26-b21c-91c01ea1c932" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118165} {:answer/id #uuid "b463d47c-d91c-5c81-9a10-4d392e054e3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118166} {:answer/id #uuid "cf5e4cec-72bb-5af0-a0b8-2346db38f458" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b ∉ Col(H)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118167} {:answer/id #uuid "65cc9e17-49dc-56a5-b839-9140f465bbd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118168}] :answer-field/id #uuid "2d44952a-9dfe-5d35-aaf5-e2dab2e19171" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118163}] :question/id #uuid "d584fac7-0bb8-5af7-99db-3f6ce440972c" :question/math-academy-id "q-34499" :question/problem "The matrix $H$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b ∈ Col(H)$. In the affirmative case, find the value of $x_{1} \\cdot x_{2}$, where $x_{1}$ and $x_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b = x_{1}h_{1} + x_{2}h_{2}$, and $h_{1}$, $h_{2}$ are the respective columns of $H$.\n\n$H = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}, b = \\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120397 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119855 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a557ee8d-51a9-5387-a28c-67ffefed55b4" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of an Unknown Given a Vector That’s in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "826165fc-f641-5f1a-94bd-36d5b21a3d8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118497} {:answer/id #uuid "b7e517cb-5c7c-5901-9fc8-4d62de0ffa87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118498} {:answer/id #uuid "d09a578d-a4f8-5169-ae0b-3f5e8801df37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118499} {:answer/id #uuid "1c9f1214-ef5c-5445-be91-c3914d8f5865" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118500} {:answer/id #uuid "20d99621-dbd7-526e-832d-85b050d0bddd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c9f1214-ef5c-5445-be91-c3914d8f5865" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118500} :answer-field/id #uuid "82d94d35-2966-563a-ae36-53ee87337d99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118496}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "573bc22a-fac9-5364-8084-060fccb61060" :question/math-academy-id "q-35567" :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 8 \\\\ -2 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ -15 \\\\ k+5\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $Ax=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 8 & 14 \\\\ -2 & -11 & -15 \\\\ 1 & 6 & k+5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & k+5 \\\\ -2 & -11 & -15 \\\\ 3 & 8 & 14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & k+5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2k-5 \\\\ 3 & 8 & 14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & k+5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2k-5 \\\\ 0 & -10 & -3k-1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+10{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & k+5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2k-5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 17k-51\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=k+5 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2k-5 \\\\ 0=17k-51.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=17k-51,$ which means that $k=3.$"}]}
